From: picowl <picowl@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] render/pixman: read DMA-BUF client buffers via mmap

Buffers without data pointer access (linux-dmabuf client buffers on
GPU-less devices) are mapped once with mmap(MAP_SHARED) if they have a
single linear plane. The mapping is cached per buffer until it is
destroyed. Each access is bracketed with DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC. DMA-BUF
formats are still not advertised as texture formats.

The fd is client controlled. Only real DMA-BUFs are mapped (a memfd
passed as a DMA-BUF could be truncated later, which raises SIGBUS on the
next read); WLR_PIXMAN_DMABUF_ALLOW_ANY_FD=1 lifts this for tests. The
layout is validated before mapping: stride >= width * bytes per pixel,
stride and offset 32-bit aligned, offset + stride * height inside the fd.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [picowl specific]
